(BAS-25 - an action-consuming construct consumes the ENTIRE sentence it
 appears in: the While below owns both of its comma-separated actions, and
 the sentence ends at the period, so `Print "after"` is outside the loop.
 Also covers: BAS-26 (commas separate the actions), BAS-32 (the period
 ends the whole construct including all its actions), BAS-33 (the comma
 is what separates them).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox BAS-25.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   7
   8
   9
   after
)
a number called x is 7.
While x is less than 10, print x, increment x.
Print "after".
